#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:108
msgid "One run: its type, status and progress, and the pages it measured with their headline figures. For a page's full detail call get-page-profile with the page_key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:113
msgid "List the current page profiles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:114
msgid "The Pages tab: the newest measurement of every profiled page with its profile_id, URL and headline figures, slowest first. Pass a profile_id to get-page-profile for the full detail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:118
msgid "Get a page profile in full"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:119
msgid "Everything the page analysis panel shows for one measured page: phases, hooks and callbacks, components, SQL groups with query plans, HTTP calls, the function-level profile when Excimer ran, and measured plugin impact on that page. Identify the page by profile_id, by page_key (newest measurement of that page) or by url (newest measurement of that URL; profile-url measures one that has none)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:124
msgid "Get the Plugins table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:125
msgid "Every component of the latest analysis with its attributed SQL, queries, rows, slowest query and HTTP time, its measured-impact verdict (adds or saves, typical and worst page), whether that verdict is stale, and object-cache notes. Pass page to see one page's figures; mode chooses attribution (code_owner or caller)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:130
msgid "Get one plugin's measured impact per page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:131
msgid "Every page and cache-mode measurement of one plugin from Plugin Impact Analysis, with the version measured."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:136
msgid "Plan a Plugin Impact Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:137
msgid "Before run-deep-analysis: the plugins that can be safely excluded, ordered by what attribution blames, the plugins that must be excluded together, and the figures for an estimate (pages, seconds per measurement). Site-wide by default; pass profile_id or url to plan one page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:142
msgid "Get a Markdown report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:143
msgid "The Markdown export the screens download: kind=run with a run id, kind=page with a profile id, kind=checkout with a checkout run id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:148
msgid "Get a history chart series"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:149
msgid "The Compare chart's data for one metric across saved runs up to after_run_id. selection_mode is setup (same setup) or all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:154
msgid "Get Performance Analysis settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:155
msgid "Sharing state, enabled publishers, plugin-update detection, measurement runs per page (one or three), stored-capture retention, whether data is removed on uninstall, the profiler state, the submission queue counts, the loopback origin address and whether loopback credentials are stored (never the credentials)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:159
msgid "Get the submission queue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:160
msgid "Queued and sent superspeedy.org submissions with their state, newest first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:165
msgid "Preview a submission payload"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:166
msgid "The exact anonymised JSON a queued submission sends (outbox_id), or the latest run would send (no id), with a plain-English summary."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:171
msgid "Get the public community figures"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:172
msgid "Downloads the public figures for sites like this one from superspeedy.org, as the Compare tab does. This contacts superspeedy.org; nothing about this site is sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:176
msgid "Get AJAX windows and endpoint profiles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:177
msgid "The AJAX tab: recorded AJAX windows, saved before/after comparisons and endpoint startup profiles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:181
msgid "Get save-profiling targets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:182
msgid "The object types whose save can be profiled, and for object_type, the editor transports available. Pass one to profile-admin-save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:190
msgid "Advance the active run"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:191
msgid "Process the next batch of the active run (up to about 15 seconds) and return its status. Call it in a loop after any run-* or profile-url ability until status is no longer crawling or analysing. Runs otherwise move only when WP-Cron fires, which on many hosts is never."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:196
msgid "Cancel the active run"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:197
msgid "Cancel the active run, or run_id. Measurements already taken stay saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:202
msgid "Enable or disable the profiler"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:203
msgid "Enabling installs the profiling loader in wp-content/mu-plugins (and the query-capture drop-in wp-content/db.php when no other drop-in is there); analyses need it. Enabling writes files to the site, so it needs confirm:true. Disabling removes both and needs no confirm."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:208
msgid "Profile any URL on this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:209
msgid "Measure one URL on this site, as the admin bar's \"Analyse this page\" does: as a logged-out visitor (as=anon) or as the agent user (as=admin; the default for wp-admin URLs). all_hooks times every hook callback; raw_streams also keeps raw timing streams. Asynchronous: loop advance-run, then get-page-profile with the returned page_key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:219
msgid "Profile an editor save"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:220
msgid "Profile the save request of an editor, as the Workflows tab does, without a browser: a temporary object of object_type (from get-admin-save-targets) is created, its edit screen loaded with the agent user's login, and the editor's real save request sent once with the profiler token (transport rest: the block editor's REST update; classic: the editor form submitted with its save button). Normal save hooks, emails and integrations run; emails go to the site administrator. The temporary object is deleted afterwards. Synchronous: read the result with get-page-profile (profile_id)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:228
msgid "Start the cache performance check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:229
msgid "Start the Cache performance tab's check: each representative page requested twice as an anonymous visitor, with basket cookies and as a logged-in test customer, then once more anonymously to catch a private response stored under the public key. Over MCP only the server-side requests run; the browser visitor-path timing is recorded as not measured. Then loop advance-cache-check with the assessment_id, and read get-cache-optimisation-analysis."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:233
msgid "Advance the cache performance check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:234
msgid "Make the next few server requests of a started cache check (assessment_id) and return progress. When the last request is made the check is completed and saved; done is then true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:239
msgid "Start an AJAX window"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:240
msgid "Start a 15-minute AJAX observation window (the AJAX tab) labelled by scenario, optionally limited to endpoints such as \"admin_ajax:action\" or \"rest:/wc/store/v1/cart\". Exercise the site, then stop-ajax-window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:245
msgid "Stop an AJAX window"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:246
msgid "Stop the AJAX window uuid and keep its observations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:251
msgid "Compare two AJAX windows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:252
msgid "Compare a before and an after AJAX window; name saves the comparison on the AJAX tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:257
msgid "Profile an AJAX or REST endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:258
msgid "Profile the startup of an endpoint recorded in AJAX window uuid (key from get-endpoint-profiles) by requesting url samples times. Only GET and HEAD are allowed. confirm:true states that this exact URL may be requested. Then loop advance-run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:268
msgid "Approve or clear a history expectation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:269
msgid "On Compare, approve a page's change in after_run_id as expected (mode=approve) or clear that approval (mode=clear), for page_identity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:274
msgid "Deliver queued submissions now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:275
msgid "Deliver submissions already queued for superspeedy.org, as the open Share tab does. Only runs the site owner already chose to share are queued."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:279
msgid "Retry, pause or resume a submission"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:280
msgid "Change one queued submission (outbox_id): retry now, pause or resume."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:285
msgid "Change Performance Analysis settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:286
msgid "Change any of: plugin_update_detection (notice and quick comparison after plugin changes), measurement_runs (\"one\": each page measured once, cold, no warm-up - the default; \"three\": a warm-up and three measured requests per page, median reported; applies to run-analysis, spot runs and profile-page, not to plugin impact, cache impact or endpoint profiling), remove_data_on_uninstall, publishers ({slug: true|false}, which publishers' recommendations may be shown), loopback_origin (the origin server address PA connects to when its own requests are blocked in front of the site, e.g. 127.0.0.1 or 10.0.0.5:8080; \"\" clears) and loopback_credentials ({user, password} for a site behind HTTP basic auth, or {clear: true}; stored, sent only to this site, never returned). Sharing itself is not changed here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:302
msgid "Get the update watchdog status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:303
msgid "The update watchdog: its settings, whether a check is running (stage and runs), updates waiting for the next check, when the next update check and weekly check are due, and the latest verdicts with their regressions. A check measures the pages of the last full analysis after plugin, theme or core updates, re-measures anything that regressed and emails the administrator only when something got worse."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:307
msgid "Change the update watchdog settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:308
msgid "Change any of: enabled, checkout (include the checkout test, which places, completes, refunds and trashes a hidden zero-price order), recipients (comma-separated addresses; \"\" means the site administrator), threshold_percent and threshold_ms (a page or step counts when it is at least both slower), weekly_day (monday to sunday). An invalid value changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:320
msgid "Run the update watchdog now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:321
msgid "Start a watchdog check now (of the waiting updates when there are any), or, while a check runs, move it on: the current measurement's next batch, then its next stage. Call it in a loop until running is false, then read last for the verdict; it does not rely on WP-Cron. Emails the alert addresses only when something regressed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:325
msgid "Prepare a fix-quote request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:326
msgid "Build the Markdown a \"Request a fix quote\" would send for one page profile and hold it as a draft for two hours. Show the markdown to the site owner; send-quote-request sends it. source is page-analysis, cache-tab, summary or compare."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:333
msgid "Delete stored capture detail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:334
msgid "Delete the detailed capture data of every run outside the retention window, as Tools does. Headline figures stay; page profiles of pruned runs lose their detail. Opted-in runs are queued for sharing first. Needs confirm:true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:339
msgid "Delete a traffic collection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:340
msgid "Delete collection_id and its observations. Needs confirm:true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:345
msgid "Remove leftover save-profiling objects"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:346
msgid "Cancel any save-profiling run and delete the temporary object it created. Needs confirm:true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:351
msgid "Send a fix-quote request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:352
msgid "Send a prepared draft (request_uuid) to Super Speedy Plugins with the contact details given. consent:true records that the site owner agreed to send this report and their details; confirm:true that they asked for it to be sent now. Leave marketing_opt_in false unless they asked for marketing email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:368
msgid "Start the ad-click and campaign parameter check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:369
msgid "Start the Cache performance tab's parameter check: each click ID (fbclid, gclid, gbraid, wbraid, msclkid, ttclid, twclid, li_fat_id, epik, srsltid) on every representative page and each campaign parameter (utm_*, ref, mc_cid, mc_eid) on home, as profiled cookie-less requests, naming any cookie a parameter makes the site set and the code that set it; then, on one page the cache is shown to serve, each parameter with the same value twice and a different value once, to classify the cache key as ignored, separate_key or bypass. About 110 requests, all to this site. Then loop advance-parameter-check with the check_id, and read get-parameter-check."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:373
msgid "Advance the parameter check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:374
msgid "Make the next requests of a started parameter check (check_id) and return progress. When the last request is made the report is saved; done is then true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:380
msgid "Get the parameter check report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:381
msgid "The latest ad-click and campaign parameter check: per parameter the cookies it made the site set (name, plugin or theme, version, hook, callback; never values) and how the page cache keyed it (ignored, separate_key, bypass or unknown), worst first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities-control.php:392
msgid "This action needs confirm:true. Ask the site owner first."
msgstr ""

