#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:85
msgid "Super Speedy Performance Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:86
msgid "Profile a WordPress site, attribute SQL/RAM/time to plugins, isolate culprits, read plain-English findings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:117
msgid "Get analysis status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:118
msgid "Whether an analysis is currently running (with progress), and the id of the latest completed run. Poll this after run-analysis or run-deep-analysis."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:135
msgid "Get performance report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:136
msgid "The full report for the latest completed analysis: site score (out of 100), plain-English insights with recommendations, per-page metrics, all findings, and measured per-plugin impacts. This is the primary read for interpreting results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:141
#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:196
#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:214
#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:232
#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:291
msgid "Specific run id; defaults to the latest completed run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:153
msgid "Compare performance history"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:154
msgid "Return the same versioned privacy-safe Before/After evidence document available on the Compare tab. It compares two completed full scans or spot checks without mutating either run or enabling community sharing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:159
msgid "Completed run used as Before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:160
msgid "Completed run used as After."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:172
msgid "Get outbound HTTP API calls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:173
msgid "Read the complete privacy-safe inventory of outbound WordPress HTTP API calls from the latest baseline or spot analysis. Calls are grouped by normalised endpoint, method and owning component, with page occurrence, purpose and fail-safe block classification for consumers such as Scalability Pro."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:178
msgid "Specific completed baseline or spot run; defaults to the latest."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:190
msgid "Get archive query profile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:191
msgid "What this site's archive pages (category, tag, shop, product category, CPT and custom taxonomy archives) actually filter and order by, measured from a real run. Returns the composite indexes those archives would use, in column order with per-column direction, plus the postmeta keys and lookup-table columns that must be materialised as typed columns first - each with an inferred SQL type and a confidence. Intended for auto-configuring Super Speedy Archives. Never auto-apply a type whose confidence is \"mixed\" or \"low\", and treat complete=false as insufficient evidence rather than as \"nothing needed\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:208
msgid "Get shared-cache safety report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:209
msgid "Read the latest shared-cache safety scan: shared-cache status, estimated review difficulty, potential visitor-specific content hazards, existing dynamic-region coverage and the plugin or theme candidates worth inspecting first. Candidate components are leads, not proven causes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:226
msgid "Get cache optimisation analysis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:227
msgid "Read cache qualification evidence. Before the Cache performance check has run it returns the version 2 anonymous hazard analysis for the run. Afterwards it returns the version 3 document: per-audience cache verdicts for anonymous visitors, requests carrying basket cookies and the synthetic logged-in customer, the anonymous leak check, browser and server-loopback timings, origin generation, cache layers, the cache system inventory and sufficiency evidence. It includes private-site diagnostic URLs and local aggregate counts, but no response HTML, customer content, cookie values or snippet source."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:244
msgid "Get findings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:245
msgid "Findings from the latest completed run, most severe first, each with a headline, evidence and an explicit recommendation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:268
msgid "Get measured plugin impacts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:269
msgid "Per-plugin costs measured by Plugin Impact Analysis: one row per plugin per page per cache mode, with generation-time, SQL, HTTP, query-count and memory deltas. Positive deltas = the plugin adds that much; negative = it SAVES that much (never call a negative delta slow). confidence=measured means proven by re-measurement; none means below the noise floor. Headline the warm (or normal) cache mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:285
msgid "Get page plugin usage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:286
msgid "Per profiled page, what every active plugin actually did there (queries, HTTP, mail, include/hook cost, enqueued assets), the latest measured exclusion delta with output-identity, and an unload-safety classification (never/review/candidate). Built for per-page plugin unloading decisions. classification=never must always win over measurements; NULL evidence fields mean unknown, not zero."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:303
msgid "Get site metrics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:304
msgid "Site demographics from the latest analysis: content counts, database size, environment, inferred sector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:315
msgid "Run performance analysis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:316
msgid "Start an analysis (asynchronous - poll get-status, then read get-report). type=baseline profiles every key page; type=spot with pages=[...] profiles specific pages; type=cache_impact compares object-cache on/off. Read-only against the site unless include_writes is true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:322
msgid "Page keys to limit the run to (e.g. home, shop)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:323
msgid "Also profile saves using temporary administrator-owned objects and order processing using a temporary zero-price product with its own stock. These objects are deleted after measurement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:342
msgid "Run plugin impact analysis (culprit isolation)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:343
msgid "Sweep every eligible plugin (or the given suspects) across every profiled page, re-measuring each page with each plugin virtually disabled for test requests only (visitors unaffected) - in three object-cache modes when a persistent cache is present. Thorough and slow by design. Requires a completed analysis first. Asynchronous - poll get-status, then get-plugin-impacts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:348
msgid "Plugin slugs to isolate; defaults to every plugin named in findings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:349
msgid "Page keys to limit the sweep to, e.g. [\"shop\"]. Far cheaper than the whole site when you are checking one page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:350
msgid "Scope the whole sweep to one URL on this site, even one no analysis has profiled - the sweep takes its own baselines for that page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:351
msgid "Whether plugins that show an impact are also measured with the object cache off and priming. True by default; false makes a scoped sweep three times cheaper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-abilities.php:369
msgid "Measure the checkout flow with the plugin-owned test product"
